Subject: Use swapcontext instead of longjmp+makecontext in async_posix under __FILC__
Policy-Class: P2-Package
Rationale: Fil-C forbids combining longjmp with makecontext fibers; selecting OpenSSL's existing USE_SWAPCONTEXT path matches Intel CET and IA64.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Fil-C-Origin-Commits: cede3de0

diff --git a/crypto/async/arch/async_posix.h b/crypto/async/arch/async_posix.h
--- a/crypto/async/arch/async_posix.h
+++ b/crypto/async/arch/async_posix.h
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@
 #define ASYNC_POSIX
 #define ASYNC_ARCH
 
-#if defined(__CET__) || defined(__ia64__)
+#if defined(__CET__) || defined(__ia64__) || defined(__FILC__)
 /*
  * When Intel CET is enabled, makecontext will create a different
  * shadow stack for each context.  async_fibre_swapcontext cannot
@@ -34,6 +34,7 @@
  * well as normal stack.
  * On IA64 the register stack engine is not saved across setjmp/longjmp. Here
  * swapcontext() performs correctly.
+ * In Fil-C, you cannot use longjmp in combination with makecontext.
  */
 #define USE_SWAPCONTEXT
 #endif
